+// Virtual amiibo (implemented by the host's hle_sdk16.c, nfp; called by the front end's in-game menu, from any thread). An amiibo is its ID, 16 hex digits (the character, variant,
+// type, model number and series a game reads), and a name (the nickname games show, cut to 10 characters). A placed amiibo is on the host's NFC reader: the game finds it at its
+// next search, or at once when it is searching, and it leaves the reader when the game stops detection after reading it (a tap), or when the menu takes it off.
