+### Virtual amiibo
+
+- **Symptom:** a game's amiibo features could not be used: its "touch an amiibo" screen waited for a tag that never came, as on a console with no figure at hand.
+- **Cause:** the host had no NFC reader and its `nfp` hooks answered "tag not found" to everything. A game reads only an amiibo's ID from the tag (character, variant, figure type, model number and series: its model info), the tag's UID, and the application area it keeps there; the ID is public, so no figure's dump and no key is needed.
+- **Fix:** `hle_sdk16.c`'s reader holds a virtual amiibo that the front end places by its ID and name (`dm_amiibo_place`, `front.h`). The game finds it at its search (the activate event is signalled, or `GetDeviceState` says tag found when it polls), mounts it and reads `GetTagInfo` (a 7-byte NXP UID derived from the ID, so one figure always has the same one; NFC-A, type 2), `GetModelInfo` (the character's two bytes as the tag has them, the model number as a number), `GetCommonInfo` and `GetRegisterInfo` (the default Mii of `hle_mii.c`, the amiibo's name cut to 10 characters as nickname). When the game stops detection after reading it, the amiibo leaves the reader, as a figure lifted after a tap; `dm_amiibo_remove` takes it off at once and signals the deactivate event. Application areas are kept per access ID, so one virtual amiibo holds every game's at once: `<DM_AMIIBO_DIR>/<ID>/<access ID>.bin`, the 216 bytes then the write counter, written at `Flush` and at `CreateApplicationArea` / `RecreateApplicationArea`, an area set and not flushed being dropped at `Unmount`. `DM_AMIIBO_DIR` defaults to an `amiibo` folder beside `DM_SAVE`; NX2Apple's shell sets `Documents/amiibo`. The amiibo settings applets are not on the host and answer as cancelled. `dm/host/tests/t_nfc.c` runs a figure through the whole sequence.
+- **Open:** the in-game menu that places an amiibo is NX2Apple's Windows launcher's (`frontend-qt/nspb_qt/win/ios/Launcher.m`, with the list of amiibo from AmiiboAPI); `GameMenu.swift` has none yet. The extended application area (Kirby Air Riders) is not on the virtual tags. Each game's own use still needs a run: none had been played with an amiibo at this change.
+- **Found on:** [Super Mario Odyssey](../../dm/games/0100000000010000/README.md) (LosDaemons13/NX2Apple), whose amiibo give costumes, invincibility, a heart, coin and Power Moon locations.
+
 ### The amiibo library's state before Initialize
 
 - **Symptom:** `game called nn::diag abort: Result 0, call site sdk+0x13ce58` in the middle of play, from `nn::os::TryWaitSystemEvent` on an event that was never set up (backtrace `main+0x1fb9920` in Tears of the Kingdom 1.4.3).
